<h1>k-ary heap</h1>
<p>
(data structure)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="completetree.html"><em>complete tree</em></a> where every <a href="node.html"><em>node</em></a> has a <a href="key.html"><em>key</em></a> more extreme (greater or less) than the key of its <a href="parent.html"><em>parent</em></a>.  Each node has <strong>k</strong> or fewer <a href="child.html"><em>children</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="karyTree.html"><em>k-ary tree</em></a>, <a href="binaryheap.html"><em>binary heap</em></a>, <a href="heap.html"><em>heap</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorCLK">CLK</a></p>

<hr>

